</details>
<details open>
{{apisummary.header|Changes in 12.0.5 PTR 4}}
{{text|blizz|UnitIsUnit API}}
* The {{api|UnitIsUnit}} API has been adjusted to apply the following rules:
** If either unit is one of the following, the comparison is permitted: "player", "pet", "vehicle", "mouseover", "target", "softenemy", "softfriend", "softinteract", "focus", "none", "npc", "questnpc"
** If either unit is a party/raid token (or a pet of one) and the other is NOT a compound unit token ("boss1target"), nameplate token, or "targettarget"/"focustarget", the comparison is permitted.
All other comparisons are disallowed and return nil.

{{text|blizz|Stat APIs}}
* Most APIs that return player stats now return secrets if auras are secret. See the Lua documentation files for the full list of APIs affected.

{{text|blizz|Auras}}
* Aura instance ID values now re-randomize when the player enters an encounter/M+/PvP match.
* Permanent auras are now sorted after long duration auras in [[SecureAuraHeaderTemplate]] (short < long < permanent).

{{text|blizz|UnitName}}
* The {{api|UnitName}} API no longer accepts secret unit tokens.

{{text|blizz|Unit Power}}
* Added a new {{api|UnitHasPowerType}} API that returns a non-secret bool indicating if the unit uses a power type.

{{text|blizz|Cooldowns}}
* Added a new <code>ignoreGCD</code> parameter to APIs that construct and return duration objects for cooldowns.
* Added numeric formatter support for Cooldown frame fontstrings.

{{text|blizz|Transmog}}
* Added 2 new APIs to C_TransmogOutfitInfo: {{api|C_TransmogOutfitInfo.GetOutfitInfoByName|GetOutfitInfoByName}} and {{api|C_TransmogOutfitInfo.GetOutfitInfoByPlayerFacingIndex|GetOutfitInfoByPlayerFacingIndex}}.
* Added a new secure action "outfit" for changing/clearing transmog outfits.

{{text|blizz|Misc}}
* Removed the restrictions that we recently placed on the {{api|C_UnitAuras.AddPrivateAuraAnchor|AddPrivateAuraAnchor}}, {{api|C_UnitAuras.RemovePrivateAuraAnchor|RemovePrivateAuraAnchor}}, {{api|C_UnitAuras.SetPrivateWarningTextAnchor|SetPrivateWarningTextAnchor}} and {{api|C_UnitAuras.RemovePrivateAuraAppliedSound|RemovePrivateAuraAppliedSound}} APIs. The {{api|C_UnitAuras.AddPrivateAuraAppliedSound|AddPrivateAuraAppliedSound}} API is still restricted, but this restriction is now only in place during encounters and during M+/PvP matches.
* The recent restrictions to countdown, ready check, ping and loot method APIs have been loosened to only apply when in chat messaging lockdown rather than in all combat.
* Added a new {{api|C_ActionBar.UsesActionText}} API and switched to using it inside {{tlygo|ActionBarActionButtonMixin:Update}}. This should fix some Lua errors that were getting thrown for addons in that code due to secrets.
* Added questID to the {{api|t=e|QUEST_ACCEPT_CONFIRM|QuestAcceptConfirm}} event.
* Added a secure delegate for {{tlygo|EditModeManagerFrameMixin:ClearSelectedSystem|ClearSelectedSystem}} in EditMode, so addons can call it without taint concerns while not in combat.
* Add the following insecure templates for addon usage: {{tlygo|InsecureMouseMotionPropagatorTemplate}}, {{tlygo|InsecureMouseClicksPropagatorTemplate}}, {{tlygo|InsecureKeyboardInputPropagatorTemplate}} and {{tlygo|InsecureHyperlinkPropagatorTemplate}}.
* NPC followers are now treated as player units by nameplates, allowing the {{api|t=c|nameplateUseClassColorForFriendlyPlayerUnitNames}} and {{api|t=c|nameplateShowOnlyNameForFriendlyPlayerUnits}} cvars to work for them.

{{text|blizz|Bug fixes}}
* ClassTalentHelper functions for changing specializations and loadouts no longer taint the talent frame or player castbar.
* Using the [[MACRO equipset|/equipset]] command with an unknown or invalid set name no longer causes Lua errors.
* Using macro conditions with [[MACRO outfit|/outfit]] commands (e.g. <code>/outfit [@player,noexists] 1</code>) no longer causes Lua errors.
* The {{api|GetRaidRosterInfo}} API no longer returns nil for name if the name is not in the name cache yet. Instead, it will return "Unknown" during that period.
* Fixed an issue where the {{api|IsInInstance}} API would not always return true when the player was in certain instances (mostly delves).
* Fixed an issue where the {{api|t=e|UNIT_CONNECTION}} event was not getting sent correctly when a party member disconnected or connected.
